 "note": "Private common IPA 723 = the delivered 722 with RPCS3 Core 921: idle iOS textures whose guest bytes changed are released (REWINDBOX_STALE_TEXTURE_SWEEP_921). On iOS every CPU texture is confirmed by a hash of its guest bytes, so a texture whose memory the title reused stayed cached until looked up again; every Call of Duty: Black Ops II journal of builds 620-721 shows the texture pool growing without plateau (74 -> 568 MiB in 4.4 minutes on build 666) and the footprint 5-20 MiB/s. Once per presented frame a pass bounded to 4 MiB hashed releases the idle, unbound textures whose bytes no longer match, exactly as their next lookup would (setting Stale texture release, Automatic = every title; COREPROF TEXSWEEP921). MeloNX Core 721, MoltenVK 6f65b2a6 and the skins of 722 unchanged. Base: the delivered and verified 722, whose receipt holds its signed image inventory. Host model only (113 MiB kept before, 24.7 MiB after on a Black Ops II-shaped stream); no iPhone measurement; no FPS claim.",
